> On that basis an orcish ring mail is worth more than either.

Most body armor gives more AC than most cloaks.  Their
price reflects that fact.  The DevTeam values AC over MC,
MC=3D3 over MC=3D2, MC over most of the special benefits.

It's also interesting to note that the prices of many types
of armor are higher than the prices of many types of
weapon, especially armor that gives a lot of AC.  The
prices suggest the DevTeam understands the relative
value of AC increasing survivability versus the value of
melee weapons increasing killing power.  The higher
price of missile launchers is also significant.

> A bronze
> plate mail is worth more than a dwarvish mithril coat.

Surprising because of the mythic value of mithril, but
bronze plate gives more AC than mithril.

> Prices are not a good guide to utility!

In the case of armor the price ignores one factor that
is crucial to me in almost any game - weight.  I'll rarely
put on a crystal plate mail except to check it for
enchantment level for tossing into sorted polypiles
because of its weight.  Yet because of its AC its
price is high.

Prices aren't the be-all and end-all of meaning, but to
discard them as meaningless is narrow minded and
dismissive.


